.TH DUET 1 "August 2026" "Duet 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
duet \- GPU-accelerated keyboard-first orthodox file manager for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B duet
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Duet is an orthodox dual-panel file manager written in Rust and rendered via GPUI.
It features virtualized table rendering at 120 Hz, zero UI-thread blocking syscalls,
append-only journal data safety, WASM plugin extensibility, and 100% muscle-memory fidelity with Total Commander 11.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-left \fIPATH\fR
Open starting directory in the left panel.
.TP
.B \-\-right \fIPATH\fR
Open starting directory in the right panel.
.TP
.B \-\-new\-tab \fIPATH\fR
Open specified path in a new tab.
.TP
.B \-\-goto \fIPATH\fR
Navigate active panel to specified path.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print usage help and exit.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B F3
View file under cursor (Internal Viewer / Hex / Text / Image)
.TP
.B F4
Edit file under cursor
.TP
.B F5
Copy selected items to opposite panel
.TP
.B F6
Move selected items to opposite panel
.TP
.B F7
Create directory
.TP
.B F8 / Delete
Delete selected items (Trash or Permanent)
.TP
.B Alt+F5
Pack files into archive (Zip, Tar, 7z, RAR)
.TP
.B Alt+F9
Unpack archive contents
.TP
.B Ctrl+B
Branch view (flat tree view)
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quick view panel preview
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/duet/settings.toml
User settings configuration.
.I ~/.config/duet/keymap.toml
Custom keybinding overrides.
.SH AUTHOR
Built with passion by the Duet Team.
